good morning dear colleagues welcome to  the second day of the eleventh annual  Assembly of the Eastern Partnership  civil society forum allow me to open the  high-level session of the second day and  today we have a special guest for the  high-level session so allow me to  present the newly appointed Commissioner  for neighbourhood and enlargement mr.  Oliver mahi welcome  [Applause]  so you're a guilt dear Commissioner and  Sara total bedlam  this is difficult but very nice  congratulations on your appointment as a  new commissioner of the junior of  neighbourhood and enlargement so during  these days we are talking about the  perspectives and the future of the  Eastern Partnership and of course we the  six countries would like to know more  about the future to know about our  perspectives we are six countries with  different bases of implementing the  European reforms  some of us want integration some of us  want to implement the core values of the  European Union which are rule of law  democracy with governance and human  rights and we all stand for it and we  know that your experience is very  valuable in this sense because you were  a part of the Hungarian team which made  Hungary a member of the European Union  and you know all the instruments how to  make this happening in the Western  Balkans especially for North Macedonia  and Albania so you know all the  instruments and we are sure that those  instruments need to be applied in the  Eastern Partnership countries as well so  we here as a civil society forum stand  for the same values and work 24 out of  24 to implement them in our countries  and we are sure that civil society needs  to have more opportunities during the  next years of Eastern Partnership to be  able to influence the implementation and  the pace  of the implementation of the European  reforms in the Eastern Partnership  countries and thank you very much for  starting your mandate with the speech at  the 11th annual Assembly of the Eastern  P